      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4494303990": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:12.898975+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Internship and Fresh Graduates are acceptable\nBase Location: Pakistan, Karachi and Islamabad\nResponsibilities:\nAssist with Deployment and Troubleshooting\n• Provide support to senior on deploy implementation, configure, and install network\ndevices\n• Provide level 1 remote/onsite troubleshooting to resolve issues\n• Assist in performing simple network topology testing\nHardware Repair and Maintenance\n• Perform a POC device health check and maintenance to ensure that the device is in\na healthy state\n• Provide Return Merchant Authorization (RMA) service to repair faulty device\nTechnical Consultation and Security Services\n• Provide technical consultation and assistance on the POC project\n• Provide after-sales User Administrative Training to customers\nRequirements:\n• Understanding of TCP/IP, routing and switching, network protocol, security\npractice, etc.\n• Good communication and written skills in English and the local language\n• Positive, communicative, and customer-oriented attitude\n• Knowledge of virtualization such as VMware for private cloud, and public cloud like\nAWS/Azure/GCP is a plus.\n• Knowledge of application systems (database, ERP, CRM, etc), storage technology,\nor Unix/Windows working experience is a plus\n• Having any industry certificates (CISSP, CCNA, CCNP, CCSP, etc) is a plus",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:12.898975+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/africacdc_cphia2026-africaready-activity-7530528458859462656-UHo5": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Opening Ceremony & Launch of the AU Champions' Roadmaps | Nov. 23, 2026\n\n\nDate: Nov. 23, 2026\n\n🔴 LIVE from Addis Ababa 🇪🇹\n\nThe Opening Ceremony of the 5th International Conference on Public Health in Africa (CPHIA 2026) and the High-Level Launch of the AU Champions' Roadmaps.\n\nTheme: Africa's Health Security and Sovereignty: Transformation from health dependency and vulnerability to ownership and resilience.\n\n#CPHIA2026 #AfricaReady \n\n\nTime:\n09:00 | Eastern Africa Time (GMT +3)\n08:00 | Southern Africa Time (GMT +2)\n07:00 | Central Africa Time (GMT +2)\n06:00 | West Africa Time (GMT)\n\nContact: Communications@africacdc.org",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-23T07:11:58.881Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ajaxmike_today-in-the-windows-insider-program-we-share-7529628206547795968-fwPv": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Today in the Windows Insider Program, we are rolling out LE Audio support for full-range 48kHz stereo audio playback while using the microphone! \n\nWith no wire and no dongle, you can now game with voice chat, use voice with Copilot Chat, or use voice typing - all without losing fidelity of the game or media you're listening to!\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/g-GDUq-H",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-20T19:34:18.296Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/jensen-huang-in-the-matrix-learning-how-ugcPost-7526476851985211392-OLOm": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Jensen Huang in the Matrix, learning how Chinese spies work\n\nWait till the end👀\n\nMade with AI by Arminn_Ai\n▌Editor’s Note —\nMazhar Pasha\n6:08 AM · Nov 12, 2026",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/josephcass_breaking-brookfield-announces-huge-27-billion-share-7523323322541969408-zmpB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "BREAKING: Brookfield announces HUGE $27 BILLION AI data centre project in the UK! \n\nBrookfield has partnered with British energy company Drax Group and AI business Radiant to develop one of the UK’s largest AI data centres at Drax Power Station in the north of England. \n\nBloomberg reports that the project could attract more than $27 Billion billion in investment, with an initial $3.3 Billion planned for the first phase, backed by Brookfield’s partnership with the Qatar Investment Authority.\n\nThe idea is to build the data centre alongside an existing power station, giving it access to the enormous amounts of electricity needed to run AI technology. Drax CEO Will Gardiner said: “If constructed in full, this project could become one of the largest data centres in the UK.” Brookfield's Connor Teskey recently said of AI infrastructure: \"there is no shortage of capital - and there is no shortage of demand.\"\n\nBig news for European AI infrastructure!\n\nFollow Joseph Cass for finance news and insights.",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-03T10:00:57.048Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/katiehelwig_oasisplus-govcon-mildredllc-share-7528479616240369665-qQTz": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Waiting for your OASIS+ award? Here’s this week’s DISH. 🍽️\nYou submitted. You answered clarifications. You checked your email. And then checked it again.\n\nSo, is GSA making progress?\n\nOver six weeks,\nOctober 1–November 15\n, GSA published\n72 announcement entries\nacross all six OASIS+ contract families:\n🔴\n24 new-award entries\n—about\n4 per week\n.\n🔴\n48 domain additions\n—about\n7 per week\n.\n🔴\n72 total entries\n—about\n11 per week\nFor those awaiting a\nnew award\n, those 24 entries included:\n🔴 Small Business:\n12\n🔴 WOSB:\n5\n🔴 SDVOSB:\n3\n🔴 HUBZone:\n2\n🔴 Unrestricted:\n2\n🔴 8(a):\n0 during this window\nWhat might the timeline look like?\nHere’s one\nMild Red client’s\nexperience:\n📅\nMarch 30:\nProposal submitted.\n📅\nOctober 12:\nRequest for clarification received.\n📅\nNovember 4:\nApparent-awardee announcement.\n📅\nNovember 12:\nContract award.\n📅\nNovember 17:\nListed in GSA eLibrary!\n\nThat’s\n219 days from submission to apparent awardee\n, including\n23 days from the clarification request to the announcement\n. The contract award and eLibrary listing followed within\n13 days of the announcement\n.\n\nApproximately seven months of waiting—and then a lot happened in the final few weeks.\nMy planning recommendation:\nBe ready to respond when clarifications arrive, and allow approximately\ntwo weeks after the apparent-awardee announcement for award and eLibrary listing\n. That’s a planning reference based on this client’s experience, not a guaranteed timeline.\n\nKeep watching\nOASIS+ Award Announcements\nunder GSA’s continuously open solicitations page, then check\nGSA eLibrary\nfor your listing.\n\nThe awards are coming in dribs and drabs. For those refreshing their inboxes, I hope these numbers provide a little perspective—and a reason to keep getting ready.\n#OASISPlus\n#GovCon\n#MildRedLLC",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/scottdurow_msignite-tokenomics-copilot-share-7528705400318197760-kYB8": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Very soon, someone will start asking you what all those AI credits were for! *ahem*....sorry Dona…*looks away nervously* 🤭\n\nAI FinOps is the new hot topic and lots of the #MSIgnite keynote demos closed with a >PRICE TAG<\n\n🪙Judson's Sunday of keynote prep used about 10,000 credits (~$100)\n🪙Chevron produced an 80-page design doc using 4,545 credits (~$45)\n🪙AT&T's demo agents jumped from $1,870 to $2,933 in a single day\n\nYeah AI can do amazing things, but this felt like a step forward from last year's keynote.\n\nStart learning #Tokenomics today using this super-duper playlist:\nhttps://lnkd.in/gbPxXVHH\n\nBTW - This slide cost 321 credits ($3.21) using #Copilot #Cowork (Auto Medium) + the new #PowerPoint Plugin 👀\n\n#MSIgnite #AIFinOps",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-18T06:52:01.781Z"
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T17:02:46.075333+00:00"
  },
